WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:03.900
- Now at 22 years old, I've seen things,

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.620
I have gone through things
and I have been places

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.999
in life where a lot of people don't go.

00:00:10.999 --> 00:00:14.810
I've got a lot of life experience

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:19.193
in these areas and I shouldn't.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.250
- [Interviewer] All right, Ronnie.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.500
Ronnie, where are you from originally?

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.116
- [Ronnie] I am from Texas.

00:00:28.116 --> 00:00:29.400
- [Interviewer] What city?

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.382
- [Ronnie] Fort Worth.

00:00:30.382 --> 00:00:35.064
Well, really Granbury, it's
a town outside of Fort worth,

00:00:35.064 --> 00:00:37.950
but I ran around Fort worth

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:41.232
and it's probably one most
people would recognize.

00:00:41.232 --> 00:00:42.442
- [Interviewer] Got it.

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:43.484
And you grew up with both parents?

00:00:43.484 --> 00:00:44.317
One parent?

00:00:44.317 --> 00:00:45.963
- Both my biological parents.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:48.160
- [Interviewer] How was your childhood?

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.620
- I had a good childhood.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.970
It was just me and my younger brother,

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.170
we're eight years apart.

00:00:56.198 --> 00:01:00.900
So when I was younger,
I grew up in West Texas

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.960
and it's around the Midland-Odessa area,

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.550
it's a town called Crane

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:09.550
with a population of about 3,000 people.

00:01:10.979 --> 00:01:13.763
My school class was 75 people.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.410
So everybody knows everybody

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.110
and everybody knows your business.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.530
So when I was in elementary school

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.260
I was acting out, I threw fits

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:31.260
and I had a really bad mood
swings, never with anybody else.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.250
I wasn't bad in school or anything.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:36.363
I had straight A's,
always top of my class,

00:01:37.847 --> 00:01:41.560
but I was also, by the
time I was in third grade,

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.023
I was a little overweight.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.220
So I got bullied a lot at school

00:01:49.065 --> 00:01:51.770
and the bullying went on
for so, so, so, so long.

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:54.900
It, it got to a point
where by middle school

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.330
I didn't even want to go to school.

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:58.687
I was yelling at my mom,

00:01:58.687 --> 00:02:00.806
they thought I was just being rebellious.

00:02:00.806 --> 00:02:03.170
I just didn't wanna go to school

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:07.043
where people were just
gonna yell names at me.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:16.020
But by the time I was
13, I started cutting.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:23.160
And that was something that I did

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:29.173
because I wasn't very fond of myself.

00:02:30.623 --> 00:02:32.750
I had gone through so many things by then

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:37.020
that I just, I didn't
care much for myself,

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:39.300
my self esteem had already plummeted

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:44.300
before I even had a
chance to try and start.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.710
But as far back as I can remember

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:53.280
I've always just had like
a deep hatred for myself.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:56.050
I just never thought I was good enough.

00:02:56.050 --> 00:03:00.490
And how come I'm five years old

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.560
and I don't really like myself.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.930
I think that I'm not cool enough,

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:08.000
I think that my cousins
think they're better than me

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.840
which in fact, they didn't,
you know, I had great cousins.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.170
We always played together
but I just never thought

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:19.130
that I was as loved and
there was no explanation

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.830
that I could give myself for that.

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:25.800
So I have, I've got scars
on my arms and my leg

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.460
that went on for a
really, really long time.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:34.013
And sometimes it still happens today.

00:03:35.259 --> 00:03:36.780
- [Interviewer] How old are you?

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:38.350
- I'm 22.

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:39.883
So, and I started at 13.

00:03:41.477 --> 00:03:44.040
When I was in sixth
grade I had two friends

00:03:49.491 --> 00:03:51.540
and that slowly went down to one

00:03:53.118 --> 00:03:55.010
and then it kinda was hard

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:59.360
because I didn't really
know who else hang out with

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:00.960
because everybody at
that time, like I said,

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:05.653
there's 75 kids and they've all
had their own little groups.

00:04:08.358 --> 00:04:10.050
And my friends, the two friends I had

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:12.150
slowly started drifting apart.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.950
Again, the bullying was still there.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.760
The cutting was getting worse,
the fits were getting worse.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:20.503
And that is when I
stopped trying in school.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.050
The cutting by then had gotten super bad,

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:29.050
I then been diagnosed with
depression and mood swings.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:33.835
When you're younger, they
don't label you as bipolar

00:04:33.835 --> 00:04:36.462
because they don't want to do that to you.

00:04:36.462 --> 00:04:39.770
It's because its a big label to have.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:43.910
So they put mood swings and anger issues

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:45.013
and things like that.

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:50.210
But by then, my dad had got a job

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:54.590
and they were gonna do
like a six month trial

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:56.600
to see if they liked him or not.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.900
And I told my mom and dad, "I wanna go,

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.610
please, can I go with him?"

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:04.860
So me and my dad moved to Granbury.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:09.860
And that was when I went to a new school

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:14.480
and this school was just a lot bigger.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.770
And there, when I moved there,

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:20.840
I don't remember kids
trying to make fun of me

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:23.887
because I was Mexican

00:05:23.887 --> 00:05:27.550
and there wasn't very
many Mexicans at AMS.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:30.610
And they were cracking jokes

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:33.060
saying that my dad was a gardener

00:05:35.679 --> 00:05:38.682
and they'd be like, "are you legal?"

00:05:38.682 --> 00:05:39.620
And I'm like, "what do
you mean am I legal?

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:41.357
I was born in Texas."

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.430
I wasn't on the volleyball team,

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:48.663
so, and also again I was still chubby,

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:54.843
so I had never been,

00:05:59.342 --> 00:06:00.440
like I never had,

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:04.150
I hadn't at that point
had had a real friend

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:06.950
and you know, that's really all I wanted,

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:11.020
but at the same time I
kind of wanted to be cool

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:13.390
and try and be popular in a way.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:17.420
But the efforts I was making
weren't getting me there

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:20.410
because, you know, I didn't
wanna, I didn't know what to do.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:23.240
I was like trying to look
up diets on the internet

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.940
and things like that,
but it just didn't help.

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:27.370
I couldn't do it.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:29.263
But by the time it was October,

00:06:31.228 --> 00:06:34.873
I started to get bullied there too at AMS.

00:06:36.894 --> 00:06:38.244
And that was the first time

00:06:39.513 --> 00:06:42.883
that I really started to be suicidal.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:49.140
I wasn't sure what to do anymore

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:51.358
because at that point
I really had no friends

00:06:51.358 --> 00:06:54.443
not even friends that
were rude or mean to me.

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:56.583
It was just me.

00:06:58.654 --> 00:07:00.948
And we went down to West Texas

00:07:00.948 --> 00:07:03.220
to visit my mom and my little brother

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:04.513
and it was my birthday.

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:13.803
Sorry.

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:18.093
That was the first time
that I tried to kill myself.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.823
Sorry, I don't know why I'm crying.

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:28.990
But I remember

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:35.046
telling my mom and dad,

00:07:35.046 --> 00:07:38.513
"I made a mistake, I don't
wanna go to that school anymore.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:41.647
Can I please come back?"

00:07:44.355 --> 00:07:45.743
And they wouldn't let me,

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:50.963
because I tried out for
the school musical that AMS

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:55.460
and even though I was
the new kid I got a part.

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:56.680
I wasn't aware that I could sing

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:58.543
until I went to choir class.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:01.330
And I remember I got bullied

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.163
because I got a part in the musical.

00:08:06.548 --> 00:08:08.480
But I tried to kill myself right here.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:09.863
I have scars from it.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:15.210
So I had to go get stitches

00:08:16.217 --> 00:08:19.920
but I had to go back to
AMS, back to Granbury.

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:22.473
And I just cried and
cried and cried and cried.

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:28.390
And then that weekend that I had got back,

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:33.390
a couple of days later, I
tried to commit suicide again.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:36.070
And I cut myself again on the same place.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:38.570
It's just this other one beside it.

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:43.570
And my dad found it, found me
and he took me to the hospital

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:45.750
and I had to go.

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:48.603
So the first trip that
I had to the loony bin,

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.893
so I got admitted to a
hospital called Millwood.

00:08:56.408 --> 00:09:00.286
And I was in there for about five days.

00:09:00.286 --> 00:09:03.470
It was one of those like
emergency crisis situations

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:05.070
where they admit you right away.

00:09:07.543 --> 00:09:10.420
They had started putting me on pills

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:13.620
and I didn't like the pills

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:17.072
because they weren't really working

00:09:17.072 --> 00:09:20.990
and they kept wanting to
do more and less of this

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:22.320
and more of that, and add this pill

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:23.494
and then take this pill with that pill

00:09:23.494 --> 00:09:27.093
and that pill with this pill.

00:09:27.093 --> 00:09:28.623
I didn't like it.

00:09:30.503 --> 00:09:32.570
I was going to when I
would have my checkups

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:34.470
and for my physicals and stuff

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:37.420
they would say that I was overweight,

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:38.810
I was borderline diabetic,

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:42.406
that if I didn't get put
on a diet immediately

00:09:42.406 --> 00:09:44.890
I was gonna have diabetes.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:47.780
So I think food was like, at that point,

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:48.710
my coping skill.

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:50.663
Food and then cutting.

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:55.453
And then they took out food.

00:09:57.644 --> 00:10:02.644
So I was just at that point
for a 14 year old girl,

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:07.880
I shouldn't have been feeling like that.

00:10:11.711 --> 00:10:13.013
I just shouldn't have.

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:19.160
And I wished that I had loved myself more.

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:25.093
I think it would have had
a better impact on me now.

00:10:26.809 --> 00:10:31.250
I think that I was a lot
stronger than I thought I was,

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:35.250
but because of everybody
whispering in my ear,

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:38.120
I didn't allow myself to try.

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:42.320
I didn't allow myself to be
someone or want to be someone

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.913
because I was afraid of
what everybody else said.

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:53.280
So after that, I did that little five days

00:10:55.682 --> 00:10:57.882
and things didn't get
better when I got out.

00:10:59.154 --> 00:11:01.390
It was the first time
I had seen my dad cry.

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:03.963
It's the only time I've seen my dad cry.

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:10.823
I really love my dad.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:17.000
I love my mom but you know they
just didn't know what to do.

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:23.330
You have your daughter and you see that,

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:25.680
they see me and they look
at me and I'm hurting

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:27.570
and I won't tell them why.

00:11:27.570 --> 00:11:31.957
I won't talk to them but they
see what I'm doing to myself.

00:11:31.957 --> 00:11:36.957
And I know that even to
this day that it just,

00:11:38.602 --> 00:11:41.270
it hurts them and it
took a lot from my family

00:11:43.243 --> 00:11:45.410
because it wasn't just
me going through it.

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:46.970
I put them through it.

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:49.853
We all went through the storm together.

00:11:52.659 --> 00:11:54.250
But I'm thankful that I had them

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:58.600
because I couldn't
imagine what it feels like

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:00.343
to have parents that don't care,

00:12:01.218 --> 00:12:02.880
to have to go without

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:08.350
because that's not something
that everybody has.

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:11.040
Even most of my friends only
had one of their parents

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:13.167
and then a step parent, I didn't.

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:21.330
So moving on to ninth
grade, I was still chubby.

00:12:23.780 --> 00:12:25.823
Again, my cutting was still there.

00:12:28.119 --> 00:12:32.710
I had had, I think, two more
trips to another loony bin

00:12:37.406 --> 00:12:41.317
and it was okay, but I wasn't
really trying to talk to them

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:46.530
or get better.

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:47.930
By then I had gotten to a point

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:49.933
where I was very cut off from everybody.

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:54.920
And I would take my
anger out on my family.

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:59.920
I would go home and I
would just throw it all,

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.530
very destructive.

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:05.002
If my mom told me no, I would throw stuff,

00:13:05.002 --> 00:13:07.663
punch the wall, slam the doors.

00:13:09.161 --> 00:13:11.161
And just because I was hurt from school.

00:13:12.781 --> 00:13:17.620
And that was when I had
stopped going to school so much

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:20.370
my mom had to call the cops to come get me

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:22.433
from my house and escort me to school.

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:26.120
And she eventually got
a letter in the mail

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:28.020
that I had to go to court for truancy.

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:33.920
And it was just, it was crazy.

00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:36.610
Cause she was like, they said,
if she misses one more day,

00:13:36.610 --> 00:13:41.220
you're gonna have a fine and
she has all these credits

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.320
that she needs to get or she's gonna fail

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:45.010
and she's gonna to be held back.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:48.927
So that was when I moved to another school

00:13:48.927 --> 00:13:50.710
and it was called Premiere.

00:13:50.710 --> 00:13:52.570
And it's one of those self-paced schools

00:13:52.570 --> 00:13:55.390
where you do like packets, booklets.

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:59.423
And I had to go there because
if not, I wasn't gonna pass.

00:14:00.869 --> 00:14:04.500
And when I got there, it was
a really laid back school

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:09.500
and not too many people and I
started making friends there.

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:13.590
I had one friend there
and she was really nice,

00:14:13.590 --> 00:14:15.523
and we're still friends to this day,

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:21.750
but there was this one
guy there that I liked.

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:26.330
And you know, there,
everybody talks to each other

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:29.190
because you know, it's a small school

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:31.050
and most of the people go there

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:33.040
because they don't want
to go to the big school,

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:36.670
just like I didn't for bullying reasons

00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:39.763
or behavioral issues.

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:45.170
So I wouldn't say the
outcasts all go there

00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:46.513
but a couple of them do.

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:54.730
So by then I had started liking this guy

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:57.460
and he was a couple years older than me

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:58.980
and we would talk and stuff.

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:02.223
I had to go to summer school
to end up finishing my credits.

00:15:04.781 --> 00:15:05.810
So I was really surprised to see

00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:08.120
he was also in summer school.

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:13.120
So my little 15 year old heart
was pumping, I was ready.

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:18.100
And I remember he started sitting with me

00:15:19.931 --> 00:15:21.013
and he was being really cool.

00:15:23.632 --> 00:15:27.887
And he smoked and I had
never done drugs before.

00:15:29.161 --> 00:15:31.730
To me, that was a no-go.

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:33.079
No drugs at all.

00:15:33.079 --> 00:15:35.880
If you did drugs, we
couldn't be friends anymore.

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.830
Like, I'm sorry, I just wouldn't do it.

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:40.370
Weird right?

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.073
Now that I am here.

00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:48.220
But I remember him asking me
to go to the bathroom with him

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:51.420
so we could roll the
joint and could smoke it.

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:53.357
I'm all super nervous and I'm like,

00:15:53.357 --> 00:15:54.740
"Oh, I don't know, what do I do?

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:56.090
What do I do?"

00:15:56.090 --> 00:16:00.110
And we go in there and he
says to go to the stall

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:01.570
and I'm like, "okay".

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:03.200
I was like, "why do I
have to go to the stall"?

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:04.640
You know, "no one's here,

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:07.999
we're in a totally different
part of the school.

00:16:07.999 --> 00:16:10.720
The teachers don't ever come over here."

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:12.746
And then he's like, "just go, just go.

00:16:12.746 --> 00:16:13.625
Just in case."

00:16:13.625 --> 00:16:15.099
I'm like, "okay."

00:16:15.099 --> 00:16:17.326
And I get in there and
waiting and he's like,

00:16:17.326 --> 00:16:21.720
